metal2vulkan: capture replay's kernels are made off the program's thread (Scion)

Upstream:  metal2vulkan, https://github.com/steelbrain/metal2vulkan, at 720ef1ce9ae2a2068999a8675717418b9416283e, after
           AdrenoMetal's 16 patches to it and Scion's 0001 to 0006; tools/metal/mk-metal2vulkan.sh applies them in that order,
           then this.
Licence:   GPL-2.0-or-later OR LGPL-3.0-or-later, metal2vulkan's (its LICENSE); this patch is a change to it and under the same
           terms. Nothing of it is in Scion's MIT or APSL files.
Author:    the HakiOS authors (Scion), 14 November 2026.

Why. The Astronomy wallpaper (AegirPoster, build 53) made its pipelines and then spent about a minute at 100% CPU and presented
nothing. A spindump of its launch showed every sample of the main thread in -[MTLRenderCommandEncoder endEncoding] of its first
pass, under RenderCommandEncoder::capture_steps -> Device::owned_kernel -> vkCreateComputePipelines -> PanVK's
bi_register_allocate. The pass loads its BGR10_XR_sRGB drawable, so it keeps its draws for capture replay. At its end, the
three kernels of the replay (capture assembly, tile reach, capture settle) were made on the program's thread. PanVK's Bifrost
compiler takes about a minute over them on the Mali-G72, and this happened inside the extension's launch, so launchd killed
AegirPoster for not checking in (XPC_EXIT_REASON_EXTENSION_CHECK_IN_TIMEOUT) and started it again, over and over. The module's
own rule says the replay's capture forms are made off the program's thread and that the pass uses the host's reach until they
are made; the kernels did not follow that rule.

What. Device::owned_kernel_ahead gives a kernel that is already made. Otherwise it starts the making on a thread of its own the
first time, without the kernels' lock (it takes a making's turn there), and gives None. capture_steps takes the replay's kernels
that way, so until they are made a pass keeps the host's reach and announces it as before, the case the module documents for
capture forms not yet made. A kernel the device cannot make is not tried again.

